cret data over a network  second is lower security  because a private blockchain network has  fewer nodes or members it is more  vulnerable to a security compromise if  one of the nodes acquire access to the  network central administration system  it has access to all of the other nodes  this makes it easier for a node to  compromise the entire private blockchain  and steal data  third is centralization  private blockchains are eliminated  in that they require a central identity  and access management system to function  this system provides  full administrative and monitoring  capabilities  and this entire structure runs counter  to one of the tenants of blockchain  technology like decentralization  now let's dive down into its use cases  first is supply chain management a  private blockchain can be used to manage  a company's supply chain  second is asset ownership a private  blockchain can be used to track and  verify assets  and third is internal voting internal  voting is also possible with the help of  private blockchain  now that we are done with private  blockchain let's move on to the next one  which is hybrid blockchain  organization who desire the best of both  worlds will sometimes employ a hybrid  blockchain a type of blockchain that  includes characteristics of both private  and public blockchain it allows  businesses to create a private  permission-based system alongside a  public permissionless system  letting them to regulate who has access  to certain data stored on the blockchain  and what data is made public  in a hybrid blockchain transactions and  records are typically not made public  but they can be validated if necessary  such as by granting access via smart  contract  now coming to the advantages of hybrid  blockchain  first is secure  one of the major  advantages of hybrid blockchain is that  it operates within a closed environment  preventing outside hackers from  launching a 51 attack on the network  second is cost effective  it also save guards privacy while  allowing third-party contact  transactions are inexpensive  and quick and it scales better than a  public blockchain network  now coming to the disadvantages first is  the lack of transparency  because information can be hidden this  type of blockchain isn't completely  transparent  second is lessoncenter upgrading can be  difficult and users have no incentive to  participate in or contribute to the  network  now let's look into its use cases  real estate  real estate companies can use hybrid  networks to run their systems and offer  information to the public  retail  the hybrid network can also help  retailers streamline the processes  and highly regulated markets hybrid  blockchain are also well suited to  highly regulated areas like the banking  sector  now let's move on to the last type of  blockchain bridges the consortium  blockchain  a consortium blockchain also known as a  federation blockchain  is similar to a hybrid blockchain in  that it has both private and public  blockchain capabilities  however it differs in that it involves  various organizational members working  together on a decentralized network  the consensus method in a consortium  blockchain are controlled by  pre-determined nodes it has a validated  node that is responsible for initiating  receiving and validating transactions  transactions can be initiated or  received by member nodes  now  that we have what is consortium  blockchain let's have a look at its  advantages and disadvantages  advantages  first is secure  in comparison to a public blockchain  network consortium blockchain is more  secure scalable and efficient  it also has access controls just like  private and hybrid blockchains  in disadvantages we have lack of  transparency  in comparison to public blockchain the  consortium blockchain is less  transparent it can still be hacked if a  member node is compromised and the  blockchain's own rules can make the  network unusable  so now moving towards its use cases  first we have banking and payments  consortium can be  formed by a group of bank working  together they have control over which  nodes will validate transactions  second is research to share research  data and outcomes a consortium  blockchain can be employed  and third we have food tracking it is  also app for food tracking in various  food apps like spiggy tomato ubereats  etc  now that we have covered all the major  details of all the types of blockchains  let's understand which blockchain you  need to choose  so each blockchain has its own set of  benefits as a result there is no  straightforward solution to the question  of which blockchain to choose however  access your requirements to ensure that  you have made the best decision  now let's summarize what we learned in  this video  first we understood what is blockchain  then we explored how important it is to  have different types of blockchain  according to the rising demand for it  after that we covered different types of  blockchains with the advantages and  disadvantages as well as their use cases  and later we answered the question of  which blockchain one should choose  so this was all about types of  blockchain i hope you enjoyed this video  on types of blockchain and learned  something new from it  thanks for watching this video and stay  tuned for more updates and videos from  simply  [Music]  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here

